# Observe the Bloodspear's +4-vs-spells save bonus reaching an ORC wielder's
# character sheet. Paired with bloodspear-human-save.keys (a non-orc wielder
# gets nothing) and read by tools/check_bloodspear_orc_save.sh. F44 /
# inc-tek.8.8.
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. The Will save line on the character sheet gains a
# "(+4 vs. spells)" annotation (src/Sheet.cpp:146) when a SAVE_BONUS/SN_SPELLS
# stati is present. The Bloodspear grants exactly that stati, but only when its
# EV_WIELD handler takes the orc branch and returns NOTHING, so the EA_GRANT
# wield path applies the component (src/Magic.cpp). A dump of the sheet before
# the spear proves the annotation is absent to begin with.
#
# ACQUISITION ORDER. The specific-weapons browser follows lib/m_items.irh, so
# "Sword of the Planes" is the row after the Bloodspear; stopping when it first
# appears below leaves the Bloodspear selected. RIGHT*10 reaches the
# specific-weapons glyph, as in sunblade-cold.keys.

@include chargen.keys

d
@dump:orc-sheet-without-bloodspear
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE                   # Auto-Identify Items
ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10                # specific weapons
@until "Sword of the Planes" DOWN
ENTER
2                       # Bloodspear's INITIAL_PLUS
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand
SPACE
@while "two-handed" n
s                       # stow the displaced starting weapon
@dump:orc-wielded
ESC

d
@dump:orc-sheet-with-bloodspear
@quit
